Description: de-assert gst_rtsp_media_get_rates (neolink fork local patch)
 A stream that reached "complete sender" state (SETUP done) but through which
 no data ever flowed (dead camera: appsrc never pushed, no segment event, no
 rate info) hits g_assert(FALSE) at rtsp-media.c:2766 when a client's PLAY is
 processed, SIGABRTing the entire process and killing every camera it serves
 (measured 2026-08-14: ~130 crashes/hour with one powered-off camera). The
 function already has a graceful result=FALSE path -- the caller logs "failed
 to obtain consistent rate" and errors only that one request -- so the asserts
 are gratuitous in production. This patch routes all three assert sites onto
 that existing failure path. Behavior for healthy streams is unchanged.
Author: neolink local fork
Forwarded: no (upstream gst-rtsp-server still carries the asserts; the
 complete-but-frameless-sender state is unreported upstream as of 2026-08-14)
--- a/gst/rtsp-server/rtsp-media.c
+++ b/gst/rtsp-server/rtsp-media.c
@@ -2743,7 +2743,13 @@
 
   g_mutex_lock (&priv->lock);
 
-  g_assert (priv->streams->len > 0);
+  /* de-assert: no streams is unexpected but must not abort the process --
+   * report failure to the caller instead. */
+  if (priv->streams->len == 0) {
+    GST_WARNING_OBJECT (media, "no streams, cannot get rates (de-assert)");
+    g_mutex_unlock (&priv->lock);
+    return FALSE;
+  }
   for (i = 0; i < priv->streams->len; i++) {
     stream = g_ptr_array_index (priv->streams, i);
     if (gst_rtsp_stream_is_complete (stream)
@@ -2756,14 +2762,23 @@
         } else {
           if (save_rate != *rate || save_applied_rate != *applied_rate) {
             /* diffrent rate or applied_rate, weird */
-            g_assert (FALSE);
+            /* de-assert: inconsistent rates must not abort the
+             * process; take the existing graceful failure path. */
+            GST_WARNING_OBJECT (media,
+                "inconsistent rate across streams (de-assert)");
             result = FALSE;
             break;
           }
         }
       } else {
         /* complete stream withot rate and applied_rate, weird */
-        g_assert (FALSE);
+        /* de-assert: a complete sender stream that never passed
+         * data (dead camera) has no rate info; this used to SIGABRT the
+         * whole process on every client PLAY. Fail the request instead --
+         * the caller logs "failed to obtain consistent rate" and errors
+         * only this client's request. */
+        GST_WARNING_OBJECT (media,
+            "complete sender has no rate info (de-assert)");
         result = FALSE;
         break;
       }
